# Wave W17-O (Route 115): mist sand — falls-foot pale sand: pale shore sand with a cool wet sheen in its flecks, the road that hugs the shoreline under the falls’ spray (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, Comet Falls’ north mouth to Copperton). Split from Route 103’s wade sand (the path that gets its feet wet IN the channel) by register: this sand is spray-damp on a dry shore road, not waded.
